---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/setup-pages.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Prepare — ExFu"
  description="Before our session: an app or two to install, a folder to create, and a few settings to flip."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="gs-hero">
      <div class="gs-hero-inner section-container">
        <h1 class="gs-title">Before our session</h1>
        <p class="gs-lede">An app or two to install, a folder to create, and a few settings to flip.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="gs-steps">
      <div class="gs-steps-inner section-container">

        <article class="gs-step reveal">
          <div class="gs-step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
          <div class="gs-step-body">
            <h2 class="gs-step-title">Install the apps</h2>
            <ul class="gs-install-list">
              <li>
                <strong>Claude</strong> &mdash; install on every device you'll use.
                <a href="https://claude.ai/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Download options</a> covers desktop, iOS, and Android.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Dropbox</strong> &mdash; optional. Only needed if you want to browse your library from your phone, or share it with other people. If that's you: sign up for a free Dropbox account, then install it on the devices involved.
                <a href="https://www.dropbox.com/install" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Download options</a> covers the desktop app and Dropbox mobile (iOS/Android).
              </li>
            </ul>
            <button type="button" class="gs-inline-link gs-why-storage-link" data-dialog-open="dialog-why-dropbox">Why Dropbox and not Box / Google Drive / OneDrive?</button>

            <dialog id="dialog-why-dropbox" class="gs-dialog" aria-labelledby="dialog-why-dropbox-title">
              <div class="gs-dialog-inner">
                <button type="button" class="gs-dialog-close" data-dialog-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
                <h3 id="dialog-why-dropbox-title" class="gs-dialog-title">Why Dropbox and not Box, Google Drive, or OneDrive?</h3>
                <p class="gs-dialog-para">Short answer: if your library needs cloud storage at all, Dropbox is the cleanest fit today. Its connector lets your AI do everything it needs to do to your library, from any device, without workarounds.</p>
                <ul class="gs-dialog-bullets">
                  <li><strong>Dropbox</strong> &mdash; full create, read, move, copy, and delete over the connector, plus per-file version history. Files are addressed by path, so mobile sessions work the same way desktop ones do.</li>
                  <li><strong>Box</strong> &mdash; what we used to recommend. Its connector has no native delete or move, which meant a pile of workaround machinery. We've retired it.</li>
                  <li><strong>Google Drive</strong> &mdash; has a connector, but it's limited and unreliable in practice.</li>
                  <li><strong>OneDrive</strong> &mdash; only available on enterprise / team plans, and what's there is limited.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="gs-dialog-note">Already on Box from an earlier setup? Nothing is lost. Ask your AI to migrate you to Dropbox and it will move the library across. This landscape moves fast, and we'll switch again when something better arrives.</p>
              </div>
            </dialog>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="gs-step reveal">
          <div class="gs-step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
          <div class="gs-step-body">
            <h2 class="gs-step-title">Create a home for your library</h2>
            <p>Create a folder called <code>ExFu Library</code>, somewhere sensible like Documents. That's where your library will live: the knowledge base, skills, and routines that give your AI memory between sessions.</p>
            <p>Using Dropbox for phone access or sharing? Create the <code>ExFu Library</code> folder inside your Dropbox folder instead.</p>
            <aside class="gs-warning" role="note">
              <strong>One catch, Dropbox only:</strong> Dropbox can keep files "online-only" to save disk space, and a file that hasn't downloaded reads as empty. Right-click the <code>ExFu Library</code> folder and choose <strong>Make Available Offline</strong> so the whole library stays on your machine.
            </aside>
            <aside class="gs-note" role="note">
              <p><strong>Heads-up:</strong> your AI will build out a structure inside this folder during setup. It's tuned by ExFu to align with the way your AI works, so it can stay organised across sessions and devices. Don't be thrown if it doesn't look like how you'd lay things out yourself. That's by design. You don't have to plan or curate what goes in here. Your AI will do that itself, with the Agent Librarians tidying up on a schedule. This lets it adapt to how you work, so your own files and folders can stay exactly how you like them.</p>
            </aside>
            <button type="button" class="gs-inline-link gs-why-library-link" data-dialog-open="dialog-why-library">Why not just use Claude's built-in features?</button>

            <dialog id="dialog-why-library" class="gs-dialog" aria-labelledby="dialog-why-library-title">
              <div class="gs-dialog-inner">
                <button type="button" class="gs-dialog-close" data-dialog-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
                <h3 id="dialog-why-library-title" class="gs-dialog-title">Why not just use Claude's built-in features?</h3>
                <p class="gs-dialog-para">Fair question. Claude has Projects, memory, and Dispatch, and Anthropic is moving in this direction. Over time, some of what the library does will become native. Right now, there are real gaps it fills:</p>
                <ul class="gs-dialog-bullets">
                  <li><strong>Desktop and mobile parity.</strong> Cowork on desktop and the Claude mobile app don't interoperate cleanly today. If your day spans both surfaces, the library's file-based approach bridges them: put your library in Dropbox and the same files show up from either side.</li>
                  <li><strong>Memory you can see and edit.</strong> Claude Projects has a memory concept, but the memories are hidden and not user-editable. With the library, "memory" is a folder of plain-text files. You can read it, fix it, extend it, move it.</li>
                  <li><strong>Portability across AI providers.</strong> Claude Projects is Claude's. The library's core, the files, is platform-agnostic. If you ever want to try another assistant, or run several against the same knowledge base, only the skills need porting.</li>
                  <li><strong>Someone keeping it tidy.</strong> The Agent Librarians run on a schedule, indexing and organising what's accumulated, so the library stays findable rather than turning into a pile.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="gs-dialog-note">ExFu's approach is plain text files with simple conventions. For now it fills the above gaps and keeps your AI second brain aligned across devices.</p>
              </div>
            </dialog>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="gs-step reveal">
          <div class="gs-step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
          <div class="gs-step-body">
            <h2 class="gs-step-title">Flip the Claude settings</h2>
            <p>Open Claude Desktop &rarr; <strong>Settings</strong> and turn on these. If the layout has changed since this was written, the settings still exist, just look harder or ask.</p>
            <ul class="gs-settings-list">
              <li>
                <strong>General &rarr; Account</strong>
                <ul class="gs-settings-sublist">
                  <li>Dispatch messages</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Capabilities</strong>
                <ul class="gs-settings-sublist">
                  <li>Search and reference chats</li>
                  <li>Generate memory from chat history</li>
                  <li>Visual (all of them)</li>
                  <li>Code execution and file creation (all of them)</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Cowork</strong>
                <ul class="gs-settings-sublist">
                  <li>Dispatch</li>
                  <li>Network egress (needed to install the ExFu plugin and reach your tools)</li>
                  <li>Keep Computer Awake</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="gs-step reveal">
          <div class="gs-step-number" aria-hidden="true">4</div>
          <div class="gs-step-body">
            <h2 class="gs-step-title">Connect your tools</h2>
            <p>Open Claude Desktop &rarr; <strong>Settings &rarr; Connectors</strong>. Connect any of these you already live in:</p>
            <ul class="gs-connect-list">
              <li>
                <strong>Library storage</strong>
                <ul class="gs-connect-sublist">
                  <li>Dropbox &mdash; only if your library lives in Dropbox</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Email, calendar, drive</strong>
                <ul class="gs-connect-sublist">
                  <li>Gmail, Google Calendar</li>
                  <li>Outlook Mail, Outlook Calendar</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Team chat</strong>
                <ul class="gs-connect-sublist">
                  <li>Slack, Teams, or Discord</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Task trackers</strong>
                <ul class="gs-connect-sublist">
                  <li>Linear, ClickUp, Asana, Notion, or Todoist</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>Skip anything that doesn't apply. We'll finish the rest together in our session.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <p class="gs-closing reveal">That's it. See you at our session.</p>

        <p class="gs-stuck reveal">Stuck on any of this? Email <a href="mailto:al@exfu.ai">al@exfu.ai</a>.</p>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Dialog open/close
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-dialog-open]').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const id = btn.getAttribute('data-dialog-open');
      if (!id) return;
      const dialog = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLDialogElement | null;
      dialog?.showModal();
    });
  });

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-dialog-close]').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const dialog = btn.closest('dialog') as HTMLDialogElement | null;
      dialog?.close();
    });
  });

  // Close on backdrop click
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDialogElement>('dialog').forEach((dialog) => {
    dialog.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      if (e.target === dialog) dialog.close();
    });
  });
</script>
